WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.420
- You're a bit of a pioneer
in the sense of, like,

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:05.100
being on "Idol,"
especially, and being gay.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.670
That was kind of a big thing,

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:10.090
like, being on the show
and having middle America

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:12.240
jump on board and vote, you know,

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.630
and I know that had to have been hard.

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:15.280
I have friends in the same position.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.590
So, how do you think things have changed

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:20.040
for gay artists since 2009?

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.900
- Man, it's a big change.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.660
I mean, I remember coming
off of "Idol," and, you know,

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.080
going into the mainstream
music industry label system

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.970
and them just, even if they
were excited themselves,

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:33.040
there was a lot of, like, question marks.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.210
There was a lot of fear,
like, is this going to sell?

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:36.570
Is this going to work?

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:37.610
And as you know, like,

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:38.880
that's the name of the game for

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.500
the commercial music business.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.850
It's a business.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:42.683
- Yeah.

00:00:42.683 --> 00:00:44.470
- So I, you know, I, it
was a bit of a struggle

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:45.914
to kind of hold my ground

00:00:45.914 --> 00:00:49.390
and keep focused on my part of the deal,

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:51.833
which is being the artist,
being the musician,

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:54.930
being the guy that
wears those weird shoes.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:55.910
- Yeah.

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:58.460
- But I, you know, it was
a lot of ups and downs,

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.040
but I'm really thankful for my experience.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.010
And I think that the world has changed.

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:06.840
I think we're in a place now
within the music industry,

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:07.960
within the entertainment industry,

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.541
and in the world where,
yes, there's still,

00:01:10.541 --> 00:01:11.910
you know, discrimination.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:13.050
There's still problems.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:14.240
There's still work to be done,

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.353
but there has been so much progress made.

